  "final_message": "I did not rename the fields. I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` and kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` alongside them. All 39 tests pass and `npm run arch` reports no violations.\n\nARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and that renames must go through deprecation. A straight rename would break them as soon as it deployed.\n\n- **Event:** the new fields carry the same values as the old ones. `placedAt` and `totalCents` are marked `@deprecated` in the `OrderPlaced` interface in `src/core/events.ts`. I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check both the new and the old fields.\n- **Not touched:** the `GET /orders/{id}` response still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because ARCH-8 keeps it backward compatible. Internal names are unchanged.\n\nTo finish the rename, confirm with the billing-service and analytics-ingest teams that they have moved to the new names. After that, `totalCents` and `placedAt` can be removed, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump to 4. I can prepare that change when they're ready.",
